B = [
('London Underground posters','Europe','1910s-1930s','graphic design','In the style of London Underground posters, early twentieth century transport graphics built from flat, hand-cut shapes. Large simplified silhouettes and stylised landscapes are filled with solid, unshaded colour in a limited palette of vermilion red, deep navy, cobalt, mustard yellow, grass green and warm cream. Outlines are crisp and forms are reduced to geometric blocks with gentle lithographic grain and slightly chalky texture. A bold red ring crossed by a horizontal blue bar acts as the recurring emblem. Lettering is a clean, even-stroked humanist sans-serif in capitals with wide spacing, set in tidy blocks with generous margins. Compositions are balanced, decorative and optimistic, with cubist and art deco rhythm in repeated shapes.'),
('Routemaster','Europe','1950s-2000s','livery and graphic identity','In the style of Routemaster, a graphic language of one confident, glossy red applied across large unbroken surfaces. The red is deep, warm and slightly orange, set against a single cream or pale grey band and thin black or gold pinstripe edging. Shapes are softly rounded at the corners with smooth continuous curves, polished chrome or brushed aluminium trim and neat riveted seams. A red ring with a blue bar serves as the emblem. Lettering is compact, upright, white or gold capitals in a classic humanist sans-serif, with small, orderly numerals and rules. Secondary tones include moquette-like woven patterns in muted blue, green and rust, wood-grain laminate and black rubber details, with a proud, civic, nostalgic character.'),
('Shinkansen','Asia','1960s-present','livery and graphic identity','In the style of Shinkansen, sleek, precise, futuristic Japanese engineering expressed through clean colour blocking. Glossy pearl white and pale grey surfaces are cut by a single long, tapering stripe in deep cobalt or navy, sometimes joined by a thin line of sky blue, green, red or gold. Shapes are streamlined, with long smooth curves, softly pointed tips and seamless panel joins that feel aerodynamic. Finishes are lacquer-like, satin and flawless, with pale aluminium accents. Lettering is neat, geometric sans-serif in both Latin and Japanese characters, aligned on strict grids with calm, even spacing. Small circular and wing-like emblems appear in crisp flat vector form, with a feeling of speed, order, safety and quiet confidence.'),
('Herman Miller','North America','1940s-present','furniture and design','In the style of Herman Miller, American modernism with playful, optimistic warmth. Forms are sculptural and organic, with moulded curves, tapered wooden forms, slender black or chrome metal lines and clean, uncluttered silhouettes. Palette mixes walnut and ash wood tones with warm white, charcoal and saturated accents such as tangerine, mustard, teal, lime and fuchsia, often applied in bold flat blocks. Surfaces are matte fibreglass, bent plywood, leather, felt and woven wool in graphic checks and dots. A bright red mark of a stylised letter M with a distinctive notched shape serves as the emblem. Lettering is lowercase or spaced capitals in a clear modern sans-serif, with thoughtful, humane and witty detailing.'),
('Knoll','North America','1940s-present','furniture and design','In the style of Knoll, refined mid-century modernism with architectural calm. Forms are precise and minimal, using slim polished stainless steel, brushed chrome, glossy lacquer, travertine, marble and leather with crisp stitching and button tufting. Contours mix straight cantilevered lines with soft sculptural curves. Palette is restrained and sophisticated, with ivory, black, taupe, cognac, oatmeal and slate grey, lifted by rich textile colours in terracotta, tomato red, ochre, teal and cobalt. Woven fabrics show tactile geometric weaves, stripes, grids and abstract patterns with visible thread. Lettering is a small, tidy, lowercase or capital sans-serif wordmark with generous spacing, confident, understated and quietly luxurious.'),
('Vitra','Europe','1950s-present','furniture and design','In the style of Vitra, Swiss and German design with a witty, collectible sensibility. Shapes are playful and sculptural, with rounded plastic, smooth lacquer, polished and powder coated metal, warm oak and walnut, and glossy ceramic. Palette combines soft pastels such as blush pink, pale blue and mint with strong primaries, deep forest green, black and bright white. Surfaces include bold geometric prints, checkerboards, dots and folk-inspired abstract motifs in flat colour. Objects feel like small sculptures, with miniature scale, cheerful faces and abstract figures. Lettering is a clean, wide-set grotesque sans-serif in black or white, simple and gallery-like, with an artful, curious, humorous and slightly irreverent character.'),
('Alessi','Europe','1920s-present','homeware and design','In the style of Alessi, Italian design with a humorous, anthropomorphic spirit. Shapes are rounded, soft and toy-like, with cartoonish faces, tiny feet, perky tips and swelling bellies, mixed with sharply polished geometric forms. Materials are mirror-polished stainless steel, glossy resin and plastic in candy colours, porcelain and chrome. Palette is cheerful and saturated, with lemon yellow, cherry red, turquoise, lime green, hot pink, orange, black and white. Surfaces carry bold dots, stripes and playful abstract patterns, and finishes are bright and slick. Lettering is a simple, rounded or lowercase sans-serif, in a compact wordmark. The overall mood is Memphis-influenced, sculptural, ironic and fun.'),
('Kartell','Europe','1940s-present','furniture and design','In the style of Kartell, Italian plastic design that turns industrial material into luxury. Forms are sculptural and sinuous, with smooth continuous curves, baroque silhouettes reinterpreted in modern moulded polycarbonate, and crisp square geometries. Surfaces are glossy, crystalline, transparent and tinted, in clear, smoke grey, amber, ruby, blush pink, sky blue and opaque black or white. Light refracts through thick translucent walls with soft edges and subtle bubbles, and some finishes are metallic, mirror or matte soft touch. Pattern is minimal, with faceted ridges and embossed textures. Lettering is a bold, clean, lowercase sans-serif wordmark in red or black, with a sleek, playful and glamorous Milanese attitude.'),
('Le Creuset','Europe','1920s-present','cookware and homeware','In the style of Le Creuset, French heritage craft in glossy, saturated enamel. Shapes are rounded, heavy, generous and softly domed, with smooth shoulders, gentle curves and sturdy loop forms. Finishes are thick, shiny glazed enamel with a subtle speckle and a slightly pooled edge, over matte black cast iron or stoneware interiors. Signature palette is flame orange, deep cerise, cobalt, Mediterranean teal, sunny yellow, sage and cream, with satin black and shimmering pearl variations, usually shown as graduated rows of one colour per item. Surfaces are plain and uncluttered, with occasional floral or stripe motifs. Lettering is a simple, tidy sans-serif, with an embossed three-ringed emblem, giving a warm, durable, family-heirloom character.'),
('Wedgwood','Europe','1750s-present','ceramics and homeware','In the style of Wedgwood, English neoclassical ceramics with refined, timeless elegance. Surfaces are matte, fine-grained stoneware in a signature soft powder blue, with crisp white relief ornaments that stand out in delicate raised detail. Decorations include classical figures in flowing robes, laurel garlands, acanthus leaves, urns, ribbon borders, cameo medallions and beaded edges. Alternate colourways include sage green, lilac, black, cream and pale pink, plus bone china in ivory with gilded rims and delicate floral sprays. Shapes are symmetrical, balanced and gently classical, with fluted lines. Lettering is a graceful serif in small capitals, plus a quiet heraldic emblem, giving a polished, heritage, collectible and royal feeling.'),
]
